{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xm3s9wnNqEnSeWDdp5twKd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-1700-batch-round0-caller-routing\n2\t\n3\tRe-attempt batched descriptor-array kernel launches for Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation, using a caller-level routing strategy that avoids modifying the existing multi-stream `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` function. The previous attempt (2026-04-13-1600) failed because adding orchestration code inside the function caused Rust optimizer interference with the multi-threaded CUDA launch path. This approach routes small AIRs to a new batched processing function from the caller, adds only a minimal filter parameter to the existing function, and keeps all batched logic in a separate module. Round 0 at APC 300 is 301ms with ~200ms estimated per-AIR overhead (kernel launch, allocation, H2D/D2H, DAG construction) across 623 AIRs — batching should reduce this to ~100-150ms.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"794cedb4-74b2-4dd2-b512-5aabd1b44ebc","uuid":"a4395948-4e41-42b2-aa6e-a841eea29321","timestamp":"2026-04-13T16:29:05.423Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-1700-batch-round0-caller-routing\n\nRe-attempt batched descriptor-array kernel launches for Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation, using a caller-level routing strategy that avoids modifying the existing multi-stream `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` function. The previous attempt (2026-04-13-1600) failed because adding orchestration code inside the function caused Rust optimizer interference with the multi-threaded CUDA launch path. This approach routes small AIRs to a new batched processing function from the caller, adds only a minimal filter parameter to the existing function, and keeps all batched logic in a separate module. Round 0 at APC 300 is 301ms with ~200ms estimated per-AIR overhead (kernel launch, allocation, H2D/D2H, DAG construction) across 623 AIRs — batching should reduce this to ~100-150ms.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
