{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018EHLL7rCfY9U19Lwe7gVpN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so the current APC 0 numbers are concerning. Let me compare:\n\n| Metric | Baseline APC 0 | Current APC 0 | Delta |\n|--------|---------------|---------------|-------|\n| STARK excl trace | 2153ms | 2654ms | +501ms (23% worse!) |\n| Constraints | 1292ms | 1680ms | +388ms |\n| LogUp GKR | 993ms | 1383ms | +390ms |\n\n\n| Round 0 | 178ms | 177ms | -1ms (same) |\n| MLE Rounds | 118ms | 114ms | -4ms |\n| Trace Commit | 518ms | 599ms | +81ms |\n| Openings | 336ms | 370ms | +34ms |\n| WHIR | 220ms | 292ms | +72ms |\n| Stacked Reduction | 113ms | 76ms | -37ms |\n\nThe regression is pretty stark across the board—LogUp GKR, Trace Commit, and WHIR are all significantly slower, though Round 0 stayed flat and Stacked Reduction actually improved. The main culprits seem to be in the constraint proving and commitment phases.\n\nBut wait, these optimizations shouldn't even apply to APC 0 since it's below the 100 AIR threshold, and the batch stacking kernel shouldn't have much impact either. Looking back at the prior reports, APC 0 was hovering around 2150-2170ms, but now it's jumped to 2654ms—that's a substantial increase that doesn't match what I'd expect from changes that supposedly skip this configuration.\n\nThat's roughly a 500ms regression, which is concerning. I should re-run APC 0 to verify this isn't a measurement artifact, and consider whether the CUDA kernel recompilation might have affected optimization or if there's a thermal issue on the GPU. Now looking at APC 300, the improvements are dramatic—STARK exclusive trace dropped from 2455ms to 1433ms, constraints went from 1634ms to 999ms, and Round 0 saw a 2.20x speedup. Looking at the APC 100 metrics, I'm seeing a concerning pattern where LogUp GKR regressed by 91ms, mirroring the larger regression in APC 0. This suggests the issue isn't isolated to one configuration.\n\nThe prealloc-gkr-input-buffers optimization shouldn't be the culprit since it requires >=100 AIRs and APC 0 only has 99, yet the regression still appears there. I'm wondering if the increase-multistream-thread-count change—bumping the stream counts from 4 to 8—is somehow affecting performance even in configurations where it shouldn't be active. Let me verify by re-running APC 0 to isolate what's actually causing this regression.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2831,"cache_read_input_tokens":52309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2831},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"794cedb4-74b2-4dd2-b512-5aabd1b44ebc","uuid":"c02ab8d9-f7dc-4692-a26c-b5611fab1486"}
