{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XgKPCodThv5YBMeSqPCj4F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019wqGWSkPXuYFUbgtiP716f","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Research trace commit code path","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"I'm analyzing GPU prover performance in a STARK backend. The Trace Commit phase takes 255ms at APC 300 and is one of the larger remaining bottlenecks.\n\nI need to understand the trace commit code path in the cuda-backend, specifically:\n1. How `main_trace_commit` works — what's the flow from stacking through PCS commit\n2. The `calculate_zero_hash` kernel and how it's called (it shows 584 instances in nsys, suggesting per-AIR overhead)\n3. The Poseidon2 hashing flow (`poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel`, `merkle_tree_compress`, `poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel`)\n4. The relationship between `stacked_commit_time_ms` and `main_trace_commit_time_ms` metrics\n\nLook in:\n- `crates/cuda-backend/src/` for Rust code\n- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/` for CUDA kernels  \n- `crates/stark-backend/src/` for the prover flow\n\nThoroughness: medium. Report file paths and line numbers for key functions. I want to know where per-AIR iteration happens in trace commit and what operations could be batched."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1950,"cache_read_input_tokens":86598,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1950},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"794cedb4-74b2-4dd2-b512-5aabd1b44ebc","uuid":"b74b9e6d-c46d-4fd2-9bc0-2ff23901c86f"}
