{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm analyzing GPU prover performance in a STARK backend. The Trace Commit phase takes 255ms at APC 300 and is one of the larger remaining bottlenecks.\n\nI need to understand the trace commit code path in the cuda-backend, specifically:\n1. How `main_trace_commit` works — what's the flow from stacking through PCS commit\n2. The `calculate_zero_hash` kernel and how it's called (it shows 584 instances in nsys, suggesting per-AIR overhead)\n3. The Poseidon2 hashing flow (`poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel`, `merkle_tree_compress`, `poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel`)\n4. The relationship between `stacked_commit_time_ms` and `main_trace_commit_time_ms` metrics\n\nLook in:\n- `crates/cuda-backend/src/` for Rust code\n- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/` for CUDA kernels  \n- `crates/stark-backend/src/` for the prover flow\n\nThoroughness: medium. Report file paths and line numbers for key functions. I want to know where per-AIR iteration happens in trace commit and what operations could be batched."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019wqGWSkPXuYFUbgtiP716f","session_id":"794cedb4-74b2-4dd2-b512-5aabd1b44ebc","uuid":"fdb2e99d-2412-48d5-9d73-00eb764c051e","timestamp":"2026-04-13T16:39:31.063Z"}
