{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D9n2HNkF2AzFa9jfi6DQUB","type":"tool_result","content":"125\t    }\n126\t}\n127\t\n128\t/// Like [`MemCopyD2H`], but syncs on the calling thread's per-thread stream instead of the global\n129\t/// `COPY_EVENT` mutex. Safe to call from multiple threads without mutex contention.\n130\tpub trait MemCopyD2HStreamSync<T> {\n131\t    fn to_host_on_current_stream(&self) -> Result<Vec<T>, MemCopyError>;\n132\t}\n133\t\n134\timpl<T> MemCopyD2HStreamSync<T> for DeviceBuffer<T> {\n135\t    fn to_host_on_current_stream(&self) -> Result<Vec<T>, MemCopyError> {\n136\t        let mut host_vec = Vec::with_capacity(self.len());\n137\t        let size_bytes = std::mem::size_of::<T>() * self.len();\n138\t        check(unsafe {\n139\t            cudaMemcpyAsync(\n140\t                host_vec.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,\n141\t                self.as_raw_ptr(),\n142\t                size_bytes,\n143\t                cudaMemcpyKind::cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost,\n144\t                cudaStreamPerThread,\n145\t            )\n146\t        })?;\n147\t        current_stream_sync().map_err(MemCopyError::from)?;\n148\t        unsafe {\n149\t            host_vec.set_len(self.len());\n150\t        }\n151\t        Ok(host_vec)\n152\t    }\n153\t}\n154\t\n155\tpub trait MemCopyD2D<T> {\n156\t    fn device_copy(&self) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<T>, MemCopyError>;\n157\t    fn device_copy_to(&self, dst: &mut DeviceBuffer<T>) -> Result<(), MemCopyError>;\n158\t}\n159\t\n160\timpl<T> MemCopyD2D<T> for DeviceBuffer<T> {\n161\t    fn device_copy(&self) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<T>, MemCopyError> {\n162\t        let mut dst = DeviceBuffer::<T>::with_capacity(self.len());\n163\t        self.device_copy_to(&mut dst)?;\n164\t        Ok(dst)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"794cedb4-74b2-4dd2-b512-5aabd1b44ebc","uuid":"93bdfe75-a49d-4cb3-b459-7ccc28df48d0","timestamp":"2026-04-13T18:07:45.363Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs","content":"    }\n}\n\n/// Like [`MemCopyD2H`], but syncs on the calling thread's per-thread stream instead of the global\n/// `COPY_EVENT` mutex. Safe to call from multiple threads without mutex contention.\npub trait MemCopyD2HStreamSync<T> {\n    fn to_host_on_current_stream(&self) -> Result<Vec<T>, MemCopyError>;\n}\n\nimpl<T> MemCopyD2HStreamSync<T> for DeviceBuffer<T> {\n    fn to_host_on_current_stream(&self) -> Result<Vec<T>, MemCopyError> {\n        let mut host_vec = Vec::with_capacity(self.len());\n        let size_bytes = std::mem::size_of::<T>() * self.len();\n        check(unsafe {\n            cudaMemcpyAsync(\n                host_vec.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,\n                self.as_raw_ptr(),\n                size_bytes,\n                cudaMemcpyKind::cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost,\n                cudaStreamPerThread,\n            )\n        })?;\n        current_stream_sync().map_err(MemCopyError::from)?;\n        unsafe {\n            host_vec.set_len(self.len());\n        }\n        Ok(host_vec)\n    }\n}\n\npub trait MemCopyD2D<T> {\n    fn device_copy(&self) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<T>, MemCopyError>;\n    fn device_copy_to(&self, dst: &mut DeviceBuffer<T>) -> Result<(), MemCopyError>;\n}\n\nimpl<T> MemCopyD2D<T> for DeviceBuffer<T> {\n    fn device_copy(&self) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<T>, MemCopyError> {\n        let mut dst = DeviceBuffer::<T>::with_capacity(self.len());\n        self.device_copy_to(&mut dst)?;\n        Ok(dst)","numLines":40,"startLine":125,"totalLines":210}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_017UNar1G72RzbDjMn1TLNVG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand `to_host_on_current_stream`:\n1. Allocates host vector\n2. cudaMemcpyAsync (D2H on per-thread stream)\n3. `current_stream_sync()` — synchronizes the per-thread stream\n\nStep 3 is a full synchronization of the current thread's stream. This means the CPU blocks until ALL pending operations on that stream complete (including the kernel AND the D2H copy).\n\nSo for each AIR in Round 0:\n1. Launch zerocheck kernel (queues on stream)\n2. to_host_on_current_stream → copies results, SYNCS stream (blocks CPU)\n\n\n3. CPU post-process\n4. Launch logup kernel (queues on stream)\n5. to_host_on_current_stream → copies results, SYNCS stream (blocks CPU)\n6. CPU post-process\n\nEach sync blocks the CPU until both the kernel finishes and the D2H transfer completes. For small AIRs with ~0.1ms kernels the sync is negligible, but larger AIRs with 10ms kernels create proportional blocking. The pattern repeats for every kernel-to-host transition, so the total latency accumulates across all AIRs in the round.\n\nThe real bottleneck for small AIRs isn't the GPU work itself—it's the CUDA API overhead. Each `cudaStreamSynchronize` call carries a baseline latency of 10-20μs even when the stream is idle. With roughly 250 small AIRs per segment and 2 syncs per AIR, that's 500 API calls totaling around 10ms per segment, or 20ms across both segments. Combined with load balancing improvements, I could realistically hit 30-50ms total.\n\nI'm going to commit to deferring the stream sync for small AIRs until the end of the batch instead of syncing after each one, which should eliminate most of that API overhead.\n\nFor small AIRs, I'll pre-allocate separate output buffers, launch all the kernels back-to-back without intermediate syncs, then do a single stream sync after everything is queued. For large AIRs, I'll k