{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QnqVRoSbLBV8UYg8wHz86n","type":"tool_result","content":"autoopt-results/2026-04-13-1930-round0-interleaved-work-balance/plan.md:5:Reduce Round 0 wall time at APC 300 by replacing contiguous work chunking with interleaved (round-robin) thread assignment. Currently, the sorted-then-chunked approach puts all large AIRs on thread 0, creating severe load imbalance (thread 0: ~200ms, thread 7: ~5ms). Interleaving distributes large/small AIRs evenly, reducing the critical thread's time and improving CPU-GPU overlap.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-1930-round0-interleaved-work-balance/plan.md:37:**The bottleneck:** Thread 0 processes all ~39 largest AIRs sequentially. Each large AIR has a GPU kernel that may take 5-16ms (saturating the GPU), plus ~1ms of CPU post-processing. Thread 0's total time: ~(200ms kernel + 39ms CPU) ≈ 240ms, which after accounting for multi-stream overlap with other threads gives the measured ~150ms per segment.\nautoopt-results/task.md:3:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-182842-15-1-plan.log:512:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-182842-15-1-plan.log:524:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-182842-15-1-plan.log:528:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-182842-15-1-plan.log:529:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-182842-15-1-plan.log:535:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-182842-15-1-plan.log:536:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-182842-15-1-plan.log:551:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-182842-15-1-plan.log:554:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/logs/20260413-182842-15-1-plan.log:597:{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_progress\",\"task_id\":\"a3c55330303e9ff5c\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01BX9kKARr8MxqZe5jFSFmD2\",\"description\":\"Searching for thread 0.*200\",\"usage\":