{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HnLMwuMZ6WpM1eGgzi5psj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-1930-round0-interleaved-work-balance\n2\t\n3\tImprove Round 0 GPU utilization by replacing contiguous work chunking with interleaved (round-robin) assignment across multi-stream threads. Currently, work items are sorted by descending trace height and split into contiguous chunks, causing thread 0 to receive all large AIRs (total ~200ms kernel time per segment) while thread 7 receives only tiny AIRs (~5ms). With interleaved assignment, each thread gets a balanced mix of large and small AIRs, reducing the critical thread's wall time and enabling better CPU-GPU overlap during post-processing. At APC 300, Round 0 is 301ms with ~509ms total GPU kernel time but only ~1.69x effective concurrency from 8 threads; improved load balance should increase effective concurrency to ~1.9-2.1x, saving 30-50ms.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hyo7cDXu8TGL7CUDxcu2rg","session_id":"794cedb4-74b2-4dd2-b512-5aabd1b44ebc","uuid":"fabf85b1-848a-41d2-8e25-80309c16bbeb","timestamp":"2026-04-13T18:15:54.086Z"}
