{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014o2C6TMYH6ztXDqg1iTZ67","type":"tool_result","content":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-13-1930-round0-interleaved-work-balance\n\nImprove Round 0 GPU utilization by replacing contiguous work chunking with interleaved (round-robin) assignment across multi-stream threads. Currently, work items are sorted by descending trace height and split into contiguous chunks, causing thread 0 to receive all large AIRs (total ~200ms kernel time per segment) while thread 7 receives only tiny AIRs (~5ms). With interleaved assignment, each thread gets a balanced mix of large and small AIRs, reducing the critical thread's wall time and enabling better CPU-GPU overlap during post-processing. At APC 300, Round 0 is 301ms with ~509ms total GPU kernel time but only ~1.69x effective concurrency from 8 threads; improved load balance should increase effective concurrency to ~1.9-2.1x, saving 30-50ms.\n\n=== plan.md sections ===\n## Goal\n## Current Code Path\n## Changes\n## Invariants\n## Measurement Plan\n## Rollback Criteria","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"794cedb4-74b2-4dd2-b512-5aabd1b44ebc","uuid":"fc153bb6-c7a0-4b71-9763-aef34820bdf8","timestamp":"2026-04-13T18:18:11.784Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-13-1930-round0-interleaved-work-balance\n\nImprove Round 0 GPU utilization by replacing contiguous work chunking with interleaved (round-robin) assignment across multi-stream threads. Currently, work items are sorted by descending trace height and split into contiguous chunks, causing thread 0 to receive all large AIRs (total ~200ms kernel time per segment) while thread 7 receives only tiny AIRs (~5ms). With interleaved assignment, each thread gets a balanced mix of large and small AIRs, reducing the critical thread's wall time and enabling better CPU-GPU overlap during post-processing. At APC 300, Round 0 is 301ms with ~509ms total GPU kernel time but only ~1.69x effective concurrency from 8 threads; improved load balance should increase effective concurrency to ~1.9-2.1x, saving 30-50ms.\n\n=== plan.md sections ===\n## Goal\n## Current Code Path\n## Changes\n## Invariants\n## Measurement Plan\n## Rollback Criteria","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
